<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robert Mugabe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1924">1924</a>–<a href="/years/2019">2019</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Robert Mugabe was a Zimbabwean nationalist who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe-african-national-union">Zimbabwe African National Union</a> (ZANU) in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war against white minority rule in Rhodesia. He became prime minister at independence in 1980 and president in 1987, ruling until a military takeover forced him out in 2017. His long rule saw the Gukurahundi massacres in Matabeleland, seizures of white-owned farms from 2000 and economic collapse.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/robert-mugabe.jpg" alt="Robert Mugabe" width="320" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Government of Zimbabwe, taken by Joseph Nyadzayo as Presidential Photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Robert_Mugabe_Official_Portrait_(4x5_cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
